%
( DEMO PROGRAM - 2-AXIS LATHE TRAINING )
( Stock: 50mm diameter round bar, 80mm sticking out of the chuck )
( Z0 = chuck face, Z-80 = free end. X is RADIUS from centerline - G8, LinuxCNC default. )
( T1 = roughing turn tool, T2 = finishing turn tool, T3 = 3mm parting tool. See sim_lathe.tbl )

G21         ( metric )
G8          ( radius mode for X: X value = actual distance from centerline )
G18         ( XZ plane )
G90         ( absolute distances )

T1 M6       ( load roughing tool - manual tool change, confirm in the operator panel )
G43 H1
S800 M3     ( spindle on, 800 rpm )
G54

( --- face the end --- )
G0 X26.0 Z2.0
G1 Z0.0 F150
G1 X-0.5 F80
G0 Z2.0

( --- rough turn OD from 25mm down to 20mm radius over 60mm length --- )
G0 X25.0 Z2.0
G1 Z-60.0 F150
G0 X26.0
G0 Z2.0
G0 X23.0
G1 Z-60.0 F150
G0 X26.0
G0 Z2.0
G0 X21.0
G1 Z-60.0 F150
G0 X26.0
G0 Z2.0
G0 X20.2
G1 Z-60.0 F150
G0 X26.0
G0 Z5.0

( --- tool change: finishing tool --- )
M5
T2 M6
G43 H2
S1200 M3

( --- finish pass to final 20mm radius --- )
G0 X20.5 Z2.0
G1 Z-60.0 F80
G0 X26.0
G0 Z5.0

( --- tool change: parting tool --- )
M5
T3 M6
G43 H3
S600 M3

( --- part off at Z-55 --- )
G0 X26.0 Z-55.0
G1 X-0.5 F40
G0 X26.0

M5          ( spindle off )
G0 X30.0 Z5.0
M2          ( program end )
%
